✅ 1. What you need to learn today
You only need four core Linux concepts — these are the ones SRE interviews actually test:

1. systemd
Manages services (units)

Controls startup, shutdown, dependencies

Commands:

systemctl status <service>

systemctl restart <service>

systemctl list-units --type=service

2. Processes
Foreground vs background

Parent/child processes

Commands:

ps aux

top / htop

pstree

3. cgroups
Control CPU, memory, I/O limits

Used heavily in Docker & Kubernetes

Commands:

ls /sys/fs/cgroup

systemd-cgls

4. namespaces
Provide isolation (PID, NET, MNT, IPC)

Used in containers

Commands:

lsns

nsenter

These four concepts form the foundation of Kubernetes, Docker, system troubleshooting, and SRE on-call work.

